cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "GeoHistoria: relative-age puzzles with geologic cross-sections"
message: >-
  If you use GeoHistoria in your teaching or in a publication, please cite
  it as below.
type: software
authors:
  - given-names: Darío
    family-names: Torres Sánchez
version: 1.0.0
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/PlaticandodelaTierra/geohistoria"
url: "https://platicandodelatierra.github.io/geohistoria/"
abstract: >-
  A web application, with no installation and no server, that generates
  random but reproducible geologic cross-sections (layers, faults, dikes,
  tilting and unconformities) and asks the user to order the events from
  oldest to youngest. Every answer can be deduced only from what is visible
  in the section, and the feedback explains which principle (superposition,
  cross-cutting relationships, original horizontality) proves each
  relationship. It includes practice and daily-challenge modes, a teacher
  mode that produces exercise sheets and answer keys in PDF from fixed
  seeds, and a Spanish and English interface.
keywords:
  - geology
  - earth science
  - education
  - stratigraphy
  - relative dating
  - geoscience education
  - Spanish
  - educational game
